cockpit: swap data source from markdown reader to roadmap_items (Phase 1) (#113)

The cockpit shipped in PR #25 with a markdown reader that consumed three
files (CURRENT-WORK.md, UNIFIED-ROADMAP.md, .cartographer/status.md) and
synthesized "mission cards" by regex over status tags. Slice C
(0d06df72) made roadmap_items the source of record: the cartographer now
writes there directly, and docs/ROADMAP.md is a projection rendered out
of the tuple stream.

That left the cockpit reading a stale-by-one-render-cycle copy of the
DB. Six hops where two would do. This PR cuts the chain.

What changed
------------
- `lib/cockpit-missions.ts` (291 → 125 lines): pure mapping layer.
  `roadmapItemToMissionCard(item)` + `readMissions({roadmapItems, ...})`.
  No filesystem I/O. No regex. No three-source aggregation.
- `routes/cockpit.ts`: receives `roadmapItems` via deps (already in the
  server.ts dep map from Slice B/2), passes it through to readMissions
  and findMissionById. The 503 case is new — returned when the daemon
  wasn't wired with roadmap_items, which would only happen in tests or
  malformed startup.
- The mtime-keyed `readMissionsCached` is gone. `roadmap_items.list()`
  is already a cheap tuple-fold; a parallel cockpit-side cache would be
  stale-layer duplication. If profiling shows list() hot, cache inside
  lib/roadmap-items.ts where it can invalidate on tuple writes for free.

Status enum collapse
--------------------
`MissionStatus` was 9 markdown-derived buckets (uncommitted, in-flight,
blocked, drifting, stalled, mostly-committed, mostly-resolved, closed,
unknown). It's now the 5-bucket RoadmapStatus (now, backlog, parked,
merge, done) — mirrored 1:1 from the daemon. The richer derivation was
never authoritative; it was regex over the cartographer's prose. The
single source of truth wins.

UI carries through:
- `FILTERS` in CockpitMissionsPanel.tsx swapped to the 5 buckets.
- `STATUS_TONE` mapping reassigned (now → warning, merge/done → success,
  backlog/parked → default).
- SDK `CockpitMissionStatus` type updated in `lib/client.ts`.
- UI `MissionStatus` type updated in `fleet-config-ui/src/types.ts`.

Field mapping
-------------
RoadmapItem → MissionCard:
- `slug`            → `id`, `sourceAnchor`
- `summaryMd`       → `title` (first line) + `summary` (rest)
- `status`          → `status` (passthrough; same 5-bucket enum now)
- `notes[].text`    → `evidence[]`
- `dependencies[]`  → `files[]`
- `lastTouchedAt`   → `updatedAt`
- (constant)        → `source: 'roadmap_items'`

Loss vs the markdown reader: per-mission `source`/`sourceAnchor` no
longer point at a specific markdown file/heading, because the data
doesn't come from a markdown file anymore. The DB doesn't know which
file the cartographer once rendered the item to. If the panel needed
that linkage, the right place to put it is back on roadmap_items as a
first-class field, not derived from markdown.

Test surface
------------
- `tests/unit/cockpit-missions.test.js` (420 → 242 lines): rewritten
  against a stubbed `roadmapItems` module. 18 tests cover mapping
  (title extraction, hash stripping, slug fallback, evidence/files
  passthrough, status preservation), readMissions (status filter,
  limit, empty case), and routes (200 success, 503 missing dep, 404
  unknown slug, GET detail, POST plan still works).
- 490/490 cockpit + parity tests pass; typecheck clean; vite build
  clean.

Not in this PR
--------------
- Phase 2: dismiss/snooze as tuple events on roadmap_items (operator
  curation). This is the table I closed in PR #96 — rebuilt the right
  way on the tuple stream.
- Phase 3: `POST /cockpit/missions/:id/plan` actually calls
  `spawner.spawn()`, claims mission files, writes the resulting
  `roadmap_claims.session_id`/`agent_id` (PR #97's columns), updates
  `roadmap_items.status` to `'now'`.
- Phase 4: SSE on the cockpit panel subscribing to roadmap_items tuple
  changes — replaces the manual Reload button.

